WEBVTT

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.676
Hi, friends. Gani here. This is Turn-Taking Trainer.

00:00:12.676 --> 00:00:17.351
Sit tall in your chair. Feet flat on the floor.

00:00:17.351 --> 00:00:20.156
Hands resting on your desk. Shoulders soft.

00:00:20.156 --> 00:00:22.962
Take one slow breath with me… and let it go.

00:00:22.962 --> 00:00:29.507
Talking together takes turns. And every turn has two jobs.

00:00:29.507 --> 00:00:36.988
Job one: when it is your turn, you speak. Job two: when it is not, you listen.

00:00:36.988 --> 00:00:43.534
Listening is not empty time. Listening is how you catch what matters.

00:00:43.534 --> 00:00:49.145
And your words can wait kindly. They keep. They do not spoil.

00:00:49.145 --> 00:00:56.625
Sometimes a word pops up while someone else is talking. That happens to everyone.

00:00:56.625 --> 00:01:03.171
You can hold it gently — keep it safe in your mind, like something small and valuable.

00:01:03.171 --> 00:01:09.717
Waiting is a skill. Muscles get stronger by being used. Waiting does too.

00:01:09.717 --> 00:01:15.328
And when your turn comes, your word is still there, ready.

00:01:15.328 --> 00:01:22.808
Let's practice. I'll say a sentence. Then it is your turn to say it back. Ready?

00:01:22.808 --> 00:01:28.419
"I listen with my whole body."

00:01:28.419 --> 00:01:40.419
…

00:01:40.419 --> 00:01:46.989
Good listening. Now a longer one: "My words can wait, and my turn will come."

00:01:46.989 --> 00:01:53.989
…

00:01:53.989 --> 00:02:00.584
One more piece: the pause. When someone finishes, take one quiet breath before you start.

00:02:00.584 --> 00:02:06.355
That breath gives their words room to land, and your words a clean start.

00:02:06.355 --> 00:02:10.477
Waiting was never about being good. It is a skill, and you just practiced it.

00:02:10.477 --> 00:02:14.599
Eyes open. Look around your classroom.

00:02:14.599 --> 00:02:18.721
You're ready for what's next.
